# python bytecode — the CI Syntax step runs py_compile over scripts/*.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# CREDENTIALS NEVER BELONG IN THIS REPO.
#
# Hermes reads every remote provider's key from $HERMES_HOME/.env at runtime, and
# configs/hermes/config.yaml names those vars via `key_env` and holds no value. That
# separation is the whole design -- but nothing enforced it here: this file protected
# bytecode and nothing else, so a .env dropped in the repo root would have been
# committed without a word. The scan that found this also confirmed the tree and every
# branch's history are clean, which is a state worth keeping rather than rediscovering.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
credentials.json
# Hermes writes timestamped backups of the installed config; one of those carried a
# bearer token inline once. They belong on the box, never here.
config.yaml.bak-*
*.bak-*
